# renv keeps the package library on disk; renv.lock is what gets committed.
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/cellar/
renv/staging/
renv/python/
renv/sandbox/

# R session state. .Rprofile IS committed -- it activates renv.
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj.user

# --- Generated outputs -------------------------------------------------------
# The rule is: track what is EXPENSIVE to reproduce and cheap to store; ignore
# what is cheap to reproduce. A newcomer should be able to clone and get a
# working pipeline in minutes, not spend two hours re-deriving artifacts that
# have not changed.
#
# What is tracked, and why:
#
#   outputs/tables/08_fits.csv        1,044 model fits -- hours of estimation
#   outputs/tables/08_parameters.csv  the estimates behind them
#   outputs/models/*_model.rds        fitted models: 04, 05, 06 resume from these
#   outputs/models/*_runs.rds         their per-start logs (required alongside)
#   outputs/figures/                  so the README and docs render on GitHub
#
# Together those are under 3 MB and save roughly 95 minutes on a first run.
# An earlier version of this file excluded them on the stated grounds that
# "the model objects run to hundreds of megabytes" -- that was asserted rather
# than measured, and it is wrong: outputs/models/ is 911 KB.
#
# Everything below is regenerated in seconds to minutes from the above.
outputs/logs/
outputs/report.md
outputs/documentation.md
outputs/session_info.txt

# Apollo scratch: rewritten on every estimation, read by nothing.
outputs/models/*_iterations.csv
outputs/models/*_output.txt

# Derived tables. 08's two are the exception above; the rest are rebuilt by
# their own script in well under a minute.
outputs/tables/*
!outputs/tables/08_fits.csv
!outputs/tables/08_parameters.csv

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
